the screenwriter of 2011's green lantern  has finally gotten around a scene  Deadpool - and when he stuck around for  the credits he got an unexpected  surprise  one of the highlights of Deadpool - is  the collection of epilogue scenes cut  into its credit sequence in which  Reynolds Wade Wilson travels back  through time to fix the mistakes of the  past and the mistakes aren't just from  the movie there are also mistakes from  the real Ryan Reynolds career one of the  jokey scenes sees Wilson go back in time  to the moment when Ryan Reynolds first  reads the script for the critically  reviled 2011 superhero film Green  Lantern which wound up bombing at the  box office so in order to make sure this  reality never actually comes to pass  Deadpool shoots the real-life Reynolds  in the head - sprained blood all over  the pages of the Green Lantern script if  you could rate the Green Lantern on a  scale of one to ten one the scene has  left audiences roaring with laughter but  imagine how it feel to be Marc  Guggenheim one of the screenwriters for  the Green Lantern movie watching the  scene play out actually you don't have  to imagine because Guggenheim shared his  response on Twitter after finally seeing  Deadpool - saying just saw Deadpool -  well played at Vancity Reynolds well  played it's a professional response to a  pretty Savage joke but you shouldn't  feel too bad for Guggenheim not only  does he share the credit and the blame  for the Green Lantern script with three  other writers he's also gone on to great  success since then as one of the  architects behind the CW successful  arrowverse so he can take a joke  meanwhile Warner Brothers is planning to  reboot the Green Lantern franchise  promising to do it right this time  but if they don't well no problem after  all Deadpool still has that time machine  thanks for watching click the looper  icon to subscribe to our YouTube channel  plus check out all this cool stuff we  know you'll love -  you
 

